  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4a404177-6aa4-4d2e-ad86-a9cd98907382",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Main",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## YouTube Video to Blog Post + Tweet Thread\nPaste a YouTube URL, get a blog post and a tweet thread back, both generated from the video's actual transcript (via Supadata).\n\n## How it works\n1. Submit a YouTube URL\n2. Transcript is fetched via Supadata. Videos over 20 min process async - the workflow polls automatically until it's ready\n3. One AI step turns it into a blog post, another turns it into a 5-8 tweet thread - both run off the same transcript\n4. Each AI node's output is a separate finished text block\n\n## Setup\n- [ ] Sign up at supadata.ai, get your API key\n- [ ] Create an httpHeaderAuth credential named 'Supadata API' (header name: x-api-key, value: your key), attach it to Fetch Transcript and Poll Transcript Job\n- [ ] Connect OpenAI credentials in OpenAI Chat Model\n- [ ] Read both AI prompts before running - they're written to say so plainly if no transcript came through, instead of inventing content"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "52d04b79-a698-4585-a0ca-62eed863a3e3",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Two Outputs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        480,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1848,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## Two Parallel Outputs\nSame transcript, same model, two different prompts. Both are final - no merge step."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "80bbf494-87c0-4c79-8578-d86e9a8dfb97",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Warning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        896,
        544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 178,
        "content": "**Videos over 20 minutes are async.** Fetch Transcript returns a jobId instead of the transcript immediately - the loop below polls Supadata every 5 seconds until it's done or fails."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
